{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #408: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $\\phi(n)$ be the Euler totient function and $\\phi_k(n)$ be the iterated $\\phi$ function, so that $\\phi_1(n)=\\phi(n)$ and $\\phi_k(n)=\\phi(\\phi_{k-1}(n))$. Let\\[f(n) = \\min \\{ k : \\phi_k(n)=1\\}.\\]Does $f(n)/\\log n$ have a distribution function? Is $f(n)/\\log n$ almost always constant? What can be said about the largest prime factor of $\\phi_k(n)$ when, say, $k=\\log\\log n$? Prize: no. OEIS: A049108. Tags: iterated functions, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_ad7365080ed38268349eec1abc02edfdce1ce635468f74706cfb0e3614d8a579","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:408","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_e61185af1b5799fd","object_root":"sha256:4b282a788902c4f6609c6d3c9efcbd0f341f2726d416705bda4caf4997e640c4","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:408"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}